<article class="post">
<header class="post-header wrap-narrow">
  <span class="eyebrow">Release 1.0.0</span>
  <h1><%= post["title"] %></h1>
  <p class="post-meta"><time datetime="<%= post["date"] %>"><%= post["display_date"] %></time> · <%= post["read_minutes"] %> min read</p>
  <p class="post-lede">SoliDB 1.0.0 is security hardening, SDBQL completeness, and one product breaking change: the client-facing job and cron queue is gone. A fresh node now starts closed — loopback only, no unauthenticated replication, no public <code>/metrics</code> — and SDBQL gains set operations, recursive CTEs and <code>RETURN DISTINCT</code>. If you run 0.34 today, read the last section before upgrading.</p>
  <p class="post-note">Every query result on this page was produced by running the query on a test server.</p>
</header>

<div class="post-body wrap-narrow">
<nav class="post-toc" aria-label="In this post">
  <p class="post-toc-title">In this post</p>
  <ol>
    <li><a href="#what">What 1.0 is</a></li>
